A||||1||Will||Survey: 1" front swaybar, 7/8" rear||||1||
Z||000000||Will||04-07-2001||09:48 PM||||For reasons that have nothing to do with handling (I'll explain later), I am about to try going to a 1" diameter front anti-sway bar while retaining my 7/8" WS6 front bar I currently have mounted in the rear.<BR>     I am using stock spring rates with stock ride height.<BR>     With the current 7/8" front, 7/8" rear the car has a taste of oversteer.<BR>     Who has a 1" front with 7/8" rear bars with stock springs and how does it handle? Does it push much?||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||04-08-2001||12:33 AM|||| I have(had) a 1" front bar and 3/4" rear and it pushed like a MFer. I tried using the 1" front bar and the stock rubber endlinks and it still pushed. My setup finally ended up being 3/4" front bar and 3/4" rear bar  with urethane everything and it worked pretty well.Still a small push. I also used stock base front springs and WS6 rears.<BR>The setup I just got finished with is stock WS6 front suspension, Held Motorsports coilovers with 250# springs,1" front bar on rear with urethane bushings and rubber endlinks. I still need to bleed the brakes(front calipers all around,88 master cyl, no spring in prop valve) and with no one to help me, I won't get to drive it till tomorrow. I'll be sure to let everyone know how it works out.||||reg||1
